<entry><title>Bike Monday Bros, November 17</title><id>https://rvabikefeed.github.io/post/8eb39d42885329b4</id><updated>2026-11-17T02:26:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T02:26:48Z</published><author><name>Bike Monday Bros</name></author><content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;From Bike Monday Bros&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;First off, I’d like to thank all of you for doing your best to be safe....&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/90f99a29c7c8cee1.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;First off, I’d like to thank all of you for doing your best to be safe....&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/c548bfdfa826173c.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;First off, I’d like to thank all of you for doing your best to be safe....&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/d8c505cbd2364c38.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;First off, I’d like to thank all of you for doing your best to be safe....&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/0c99858ae691bcd2.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;First off, I’d like to thank all of you for doing your best to be safe....&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/e68cddb3114a5d6f.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;First off, I’d like to thank all of you for doing your best to be safe....&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; src=&quot;https://rvabikefeed.github.io/images/97c3d6b9917cc46c.jpg&quot;/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;First off, I’d like to thank all of you for doing your best to be safe.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
That said, the incident tonight with the angry driver was a situation that has become all to fckn familiar in this country, where a frustrated, angry driver decides they want to endanger cyclists because they are inconvenienced for a block or a few minutes. &lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
Well tonight, that driver met consequences. &lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
We saw where she parked and we approached her. Some of us had some choice words that told her in no uncertain terms, you are dangerous and we don’t like it.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
But, after everyone left and continued on with the ride, I decided to have a conversation with her. Mostly to let her know OUR point of view and key her into the logistics of  large rides and how we always consider cars out of caution.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
In the end, I did the best I could to explain, but you can only get some people so far. We shook hands, I gave her my card incase she wanted to talk more about it, we shook hands and wished her a good night.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
Though, I don’t know about her, we continued to have a good night. A few mechanicals, lots of laughs and conversations and a little dancing.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
Thanx all of you who braved the cold and came out. &lt;br/&gt;
Sorry for the long post… TLDR I know. &lt;br/&gt;
Have a great week, be safe and we’ll see you Monday! &lt;br/&gt;
😁🚲❤️#bikemondaybros</content></entry>
